<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 16 in A major, finale (Friedrich Witt)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1790s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">What Is to Be Done? (Nikolay Chernyshevsky)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">a song with the refrain sung in the novel</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">French version of Chernyshevsky's song (translator &quot;A.T.&quot;)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1875</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as, later reproduced in Benjamin Tucker's translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 6 &quot;Revolutionary&quot; (Nikolai Myaskovsky)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1923</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Si Versailles m'était conté, sung by Édith Piaf</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1954</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ah! das geht ran (Gerd Semmer, sung by Dieter Süverkrüp)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1962</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Scarlet Pimpernel (television series)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1999</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in English</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Napoleon (Ridley Scott film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2023</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Piaf's version used</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Mea Culpa (Ah! Ça ira!) (Gojira and Marina Viotti)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2024</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new version</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Le carillon national (Jean-Antoine Bécourt)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the contredanse tune it is sung to</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Benjamin Franklin's saying &quot;Ça ira&quot;</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1776–1785</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the title and refrain</span></li></ul></section>
